  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nIt is a gorgeous day with temperatures feeling a full 15 to 20 \ndegrees cooler than this time yesterday. Temperatures tomorrow will \ntop out in the upper 70s to near 80. If MSP doesn't hit 80 tomorrow, \nit will be the first day to have a sub 80 high since June 26th. \nNorthwest flow aloft will continue to advect dry air into the region \nthrough early Thursday. Ridging will slowly start to move into the \nCentral Plains by the end of the week, allowing temperatures to \ncreep up into the mid 80s. Heat and humidity returns with a\nvengeance come Saturday. Dew points will jump back into the \nupper 60s to low 70s and highs in the 90s returning through \nearly next week. The aforementioned ridge will remain centered \nfar enough to the south that any waves along the periphery \ncould bring some rain chances. However, the majority of the \nforecast period looks to remain dry. Enjoy the break from the \nheat!",
